.TH PQ VI 8/24/77
.SH NAME
pq \- print quota
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pq
[ dirname ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Pq
searches up the path from your current directory and finds the nearest
quota file.
It then prints the used and maximum quota of this quota file,
and expresses this as a percentage.
This is useful when you are several levels deep in your account and wish to
find out what your quota is.
.sp
If
.I dirname
is specified,
.I pq
will look in that directory for a ".q" file,
and report on that.
.SH AUTHOR
Kurt Shoens, Ken Arnold
.SH BUGS
.I Pq
should find the most restrictive quota on the path to the root
and print that, perhaps with its name, ala
.I pwd.
